tation/Traversal/EdgeDepthFirstSearch/suffix(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearch\/suffix(_:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"suffix","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":") -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/traversal\/edgedepthfirstsearch\/suffix(_:)","type":"topic","title":"suffix(_:)"},"doc://Traversal/documentation/Traversal/EdgeDepthFirstSearch":{"abstract":[{"text":"A depth-first search whose edge events carry edge positions: a sequence of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent"},{"text":"s, in the order ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DepthFirstSearch"},{"text":" reports them, with every edge","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"classified as a tree, back, forward or cross edge. Parallel edges are told apart: a repeated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tree edge is a forward edge at its own position. It holds a copy of the graph and can be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterated more than once. The search keeps its own stack, so a deep graph cannot overflow the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"call stack.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearch","title":"EdgeDepthFirstSearch","url":"\/documentation\/traversal\/edgedepthfirstsearch","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EdgeDepthFirstSearch","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EdgeDepthFirstSearch",